      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<vector<int>> blockedColumns(n);\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int row, column;\n        cin >> row >> column;\n        blockedColumns[row].push_back(column);\n    }\n\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n\n    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n        vector<int>& obstacles = blockedColumns[row];\n        sort(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end());\n        obstacles.erase(unique(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end()), obstacles.end());\n\n        int column = 0;\n        int left = 0;\n        for (int blocked : obstacles) {\n            for (; column < blocked; ++column) {\n                int value = dp[column] + left;\n                if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n                dp[column] = value;\n                left = value;\n            }\n            dp[blocked] = 0;\n            left = 0;\n            column = blocked + 1;\n        }\n        for (; column < n; ++column) {\n            int value = dp[column] + left;\n            if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n            dp[column] = value;\n            left = value;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "A single contiguous DP row and sorted obstacle lists should reduce memory traffic by eliminating row copies, quadratic obstacle storage, and obstacle checks inside clear spans.",
  "notes": "Portable scalar candidate for ARM64. Preserves duplicate-obstacle semantics and single-cell cases. No commands or measurements were performed; correctness and speed remain for controller evaluation.",
